Camera roll from Barossa Valley—one of Australia’s gorgeous wine regions, about an hour’s drive from Adelaide in South Australia. 

It’s known for its rolling hills, golden vineyards, charming stone cottages, and peaceful country roads lined with gum trees. 

We saw kangaroos hopping around, herds of sheep, cows, goats and horses!!

The wine was incredible (new favourite is Granache!), the food was farm-to-table and the shops were sooo lovely!! 

A few favourites:
@maggiebeerfarmshop 
@yalumbawine 
@jacobscreekwine 
@chateautanunda 
@theloftbarossa 
@vassevirgin 

Barossa reminded me how full life feels when you savour it slowly over a cozy couple of days!!!

Add it to your list if you are visiting Australia! I can’t wait to go back.

I was supposed to be in the East Coast for a little work and a little fun, but I think I needed the break so much that it ended up being more rest, nature and slowing down to truly unwind. It was the perfect 4 day getaway. 

Here’s my list of recommendations! Save for your next east coast trip. 

RESTAURANTS 🍽️ 
@barkismet for dinner
@cafelunette.hfx for aprés a midi (I recommend their espresso martini and frites)
@highwaymanhfx for happy hour (order the charcuterie board—best pan con tomate)
@waterpolohfx for dinner— gorgeous restaurant that makes you feel like you’re dining on a giant yacht 
@veranohfx for breakfast/brunch

COFFEE & TREATS ☕️ 
@weirdharbour —great lattes and the friendliest service!
@sevenbays 
@bramble.hfx for vegan treats—their donuts are fantastic
@cowsicecream for blueberry ice cream! 

THINGS TO DO 🌳 
@theinterludespa downtown for a massage and get the add-on pass for the amenities at the gorgeous new @muirhotelhalifax 

Walk through Point Pleasant Park
Do an evening stroll along the waterfront 

Hike Cape Split—this is 4 hours in total so be prepared! Head to a few wineries after. Our favourite was @lwwines where we tried Tidal Bay, enjoyed the best snacks and then had wood-fired pizza with a beautiful view 

I actually want to spend more time in Wolfville on my next visit, it’s so quaint and charming! 

Other recs I didn’t get to do this time:
@daryahalifax 
@drifthalifax for espresso martinis
@ednarestaurant 
@thewoodenmonkeyrestaurants 

Anything I missed?! Share your recs with me cause I’ll be going back!

